cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "2-D DWT architectures for image decomposition"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Khalili Sadaghiani"
    given-names: "Abdolvahab"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4870-2768"
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical Engineering, Linköping University, Linköping, Sweden"
repository-code: "https://github.com/VKHS/2D-DWT-architectures-for-Image-decomposition"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Six schedules of the separable 2-D CDF 5/3 discrete wavelet transform
  (row-column FIR, fused lifting, direct 2-D, five-row line buffer,
  halo-tiled 2-D and folded lifting) in Python, MATLAB and parameterised
  Verilog, with an exact integer (Q6) arithmetic contract, an independent
  integer oracle, a cycle-accurate model of the RTL and an illustrated
  hardware handbook.
keywords:
  - discrete wavelet transform
  - CDF 5/3
  - lifting scheme
  - image decomposition
  - VLSI architecture
  - FPGA
  - Verilog
